<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#measles">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Measles</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Measles is a highly contagious viral disease. Introduced to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> by Europeans, it caused devastating epidemics among indigenous populations who had no immunity. Along with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a> and other diseases, it contributed to the catastrophic population decline that accompanied the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>'s conquests.</p></div>
